bug_report:
Temporaries evaluated for arguments of a default constructors of array elements not destructed properly (?)
This testcase outputs a surprising result:

struct A {
  A() { std::cout << "C" << std::endl; }
  ~A() { std::cout << "D" << std::endl; }
};

struct B {
  B(A const& a = A()) { }
};

typedef B array[2];

int main() {
  array{};
}

GCC prints "CCDD". I would have expected "CDCD", as it seems that is the intent of the wording in the spec (FDIS). The FDIS however seems to be contradicting here, but it appears to me that GCC should better print "CDCD", so as to follow the intent. 

Originated fromhttp://stackoverflow.com/questions/6315670/when-an-array-is-created-by-a-subexpression-what-happens-with-the-temporaries-th.
